WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.980
We, the Strange Power
 Risk Management Office,

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:08.480
have inspected Misterious-Sword Claude
 by request of the police.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.160
How many superhuman corpses
 were at the island?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.580
Most of the corpses were Japanese.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.830
Most were in their teens,
 and there was one that looked under 7.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.910
There were over 100 in all.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.670
Those found at Hokkaido were
 probably transferred from there.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:32.750
Japan's Superhuman Bureau
 may have taken part in it.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.080
Write it and we'll bag you
 under the Secret Functional Law.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.890
This is about human rights!

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.120
Stop this press conference.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.120
I requested them to
 investigate the truth.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:05.250
Concrete Revolutio
 ~Superhuman Phantasmagoria~

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.370
I heard it
 A voice cursing fate

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.540
I found it
 A way to use my power

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:21.330
What you want are not words,
 are they?

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.700
That love inside
 I want to send it on

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:27.450
Justice is not on my side

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:31.870
The only thing absolute for me
 is myself

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:34.330
Come on Wakers. Ready, go!

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:39.370
Protecting the illusions
 that somebody dreamed of

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:43.870
will liberate the stagnant sky

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.540
We hurl our unanswerable cries
 at each other

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:54.370
And they become the reason we live

00:01:55.160 --> 00:02:00.040
What can I do in this
 hopeless world we live in?

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:05.160
Only those that keep searching

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.040
can become the future

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:12.000
Start the revolution!

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.500
(Secret Lab in Ogasawara
 by Japan and U.S.)

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.240
(Human Experiments?
 Protests Across the Nation)

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:26.250
(Shinjuku Riot)

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.330
Claude.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.750
Jin Nagakawa wanted
 to bring this to light.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.620
I've told you.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.580
We knew nothing about
 the labs in Ogasawara.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:41.140
How about the boss being
 something like cigarette smoke?

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:45.140
Was there a problem
 with him being an alien?

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:47.410
You'd been hiding it.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.500
About Rainbow Knight too.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:53.080
You let Claude and Hoshino go
 because you believed him?

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.620
I didn't let them go.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:57.150
Jin... I will find Claude.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:58.910
Kikko too.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.870
Two months.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.540
Deal with it before the Revised Secret
 Functional Law passes.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:06.830
Avenge the boss.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.910
The rest comes later.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.250
(October 21st, the 43rd of Shinka Era,
 Tokyo)

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.470
The derailment accident that happened
 last August at Shinjuku.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.350
We found that the U.S.'s military fuel
 was transported through the city.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:27.910
And last October.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.120
Superhumans and the police
 clashed at Haneda Airport.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.900
A student died.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:40.080
And the superhuman experiments
 at Bonin exposed this summer.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:44.280
This was the last straw,
 and young people are in a rage now.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.280
(Stop U.S. Tankers)

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:48.410
October, the 43rd of Shinka Era.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.370
Young people across the world
 are standing up.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.290
It will go down in history.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.200
Anti-war rallies in the U.S.
 Student uprisings in Paris and Berlin.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.300
There's more.

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:04.050
Milan. Rome. Athens.
 Istanbul. Belgrade.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.970
London. Mexico City. Barcelona.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.180
Amsterdam. Tel Aviv.
 Warsaw. And Prague.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:15.870
Young people around the world
 are taking a stand all at once.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.910
They're confronting authority.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.370
And at Tokyo.
 Today, the World Peace Memorial Day.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:24.080
A massive rally is scheduled
 to take place.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:30.330
They're saying they'll stop the U.S.'s
 superhuman cargo train at Shinjuku.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.370
Will that change anything?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.000
The world changing is just a fantasy.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.540
It won't be just Shinjuku Station.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.950
The Ministry of Defense and
 the National Diet too.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.000
There might even be
 an armed revolution tonight.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.160
But the government won
 at Prague and Paris.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.950
But Tokyo has Claude.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.080
So you're saying to vote against
 the Revised Secret Functional Law.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.860
You guys just want to make
 a superhuman idol and make profit.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:04.370
But with the revision,
 superhumans will get registered.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.290
You private companies
 won't have your way.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:12.160
Ad agencies only think about
 profiting off others.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.910
But you must want to control
 dangerous persons.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.790
Read the articles.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:23.620
Listen. The revised laws will
 specify humans and non-humans.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.450
Once someone is recognized as
 a superhuman, human laws won't apply.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.290
Criminals-to-be, dangerous ideologies,
 race differences.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:36.410
Defining them as superhumans
 allows for any sort of isolation.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:41.620
I'd never even thought about that.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.860
What the heck's the Bureau for?

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.660
You still can't find Claude
 after two months?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.370
Kill him and the witch tonight.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.200
I was mistaken.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:06.130
Akita?

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.390
Is it you, Akita?

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:23.250
The 8th of this month, a certain sect
 opposed U.S.'s fuel transportation.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:28.410
They held an electric music rally
 against U.S. tankers and law revision.

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.620
On World Peace Memorial Day
 on the 21st,

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.080
more people are expected.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.660
I didn't think you'd show up.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.250
We are not enemies
 like Hitoyoshi and Hoshinoko.

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.500
Oh. But you tagged up with Claude.

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:48.410
If Claude and Hoshinoko make
 a contract, this world will stabilize.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:49.580
So that's why.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:54.330
Actually, I've also been
 looking for a partner.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.600
Plain humans aren't enough for me.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.500
But you...

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.480
Ullr is in tears...

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.370
The Queen of the Demon's World, huh.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.000
Humans...

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:17.200
For her, they're only tools
 to suck happy energy from.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:20.040
A cold-blooded personality
 lay dormant in her.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.870
The drug that Jin Nagakawa
 had prepared...

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:26.500
Claude's strong hypnosis...

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:30.590
And her disappointment in you
 all woke it up.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.290
Is there a way to restore her?

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:36.700
No.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:37.970
Of course not.

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.480
That's her true identity.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:48.910
But you'll still fight Claude.
 For Kikko-chan.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.320
- Darn.
 - What is it?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.750
Do you know about the Jinko?

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:59.040
The human tiger?

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.580
Humans become tigers.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:03.250
It's legend of people becoming tigers

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:07.000
from being possessed by desire
 or excessive loneliness.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.700
That's a Yokai too.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:09.790
So?

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:11.670
Turn Kikko into a Jinko.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.970
Just the part that's
 Queen of the Demon's World.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.720
It's just being activated
 by the drug now.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.120
The other Kikko-chan
 that you know of...

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:24.370
She'll remain?

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:27.410
Yes, if it really is
 a true part of her.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:29.610
But promise me, Jiro.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.610
Don't ever see her again after this.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.750
You try to be who she desires
 when you're with her.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.000
As if you could save all superhumans.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:08:59.910
They're coming!

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.020
Claude is among the students.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.370
Anybody that resembles him...

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.650
Capture them all.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:14.790
They'll gain Shinjuku Station,
 and Claude will become a great star.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.530
All superhumans will revolt,

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.250
and change this nation.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.950
Let's do it.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:25.500
Yeah.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.830
Everybody, helmets on!

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.540
We're Claude!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.120
We're all Claude!

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:43.540
Onlookers gathered before
 the protestors did at Shinjuku.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.120
Over 20,000 people...

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:47.370
It's like they just want to riot.

00:09:47.410 --> 00:09:49.870
I don't know much about it but...

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:51.450
It's simple.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:54.790
All the students
 were born after the war.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:58.540
So they've grown up
 listening to their parents.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:01.870
Like, no more wars or fascism.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.250
I see.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.540
Adults forget about it easily.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.790
For students,
 that's justice from their parents.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.580
It's the Angel Stars!

00:10:11.620 --> 00:10:14.250
They're performing among the students.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:19.720
Put your lips together
 and be fascinated.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:27.310
The U.S. said they'd cancelled
 the tank carrier long ago.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:31.250
But why are the students
 still gathered here?

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.250
I leaked info.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:37.000
That the tank will still
 come to Shinjuku Station.

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:39.200
You gathered them on purpose?

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.540
Chaos at the East Exit!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.160
You're going?

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.790
The students are angry
 for us superhumans.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.790
But there's superhuman police.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:55.250
Superhumans fighting each other?

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.410
Earth-chan.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:04.720
Which side are you on?

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.910
This is not funny.

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:15.860
Are you really going?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.120
The Security Force is there.

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.360
Claude is waiting.

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:20.750
I know it.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:23.410
- Yoyogi Station.
 - Let's get off.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.790
This isn't Shinjuku.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.080
They're coming.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.250
They penetrated the East Exit gate?

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.370
No, they came on the tracks
 from Yoyogi.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:41.720
They have all the weapons they need.

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:53.060
Stop!

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:57.790
Earth-chan! Which side are you on?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.650
If you'll still fight,
 I'll beat you both!

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.660
I'm sick of tragedies like Haneda.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.370
Earth-chan!

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.160
Violent students are at fault.

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:16.040
Otonashi Yumihiko.
 Are you on the police's side?

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:19.590
That's right.
 Justice is better when it's clear.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:21.830
Right, Earth-chan?

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:24.870
I saw a dream.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.470
It's for that dream.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:28.970
Superhuman detective.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.580
It's too dangerous
 for children's play.

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.790
Please move.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:42.790
Taking over Shinjuku
 to stop the U.S.'s tank?

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.830
More like bothering
 thousands of commuters.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:47.450
Superhumans...

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:50.700
We aren't for fighting
 petty evils in the dark.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:53.910
We need to join forces
 and change the world.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.410
Claude is an evil mutant.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:02.290
The superhuman experiments of the U.S.
 and the government are unforgivable.

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:04.660
Somebody has to say it.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.200
Hurry, Kicker!

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.830
Fuurouta, thanks.

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.200
Guys!

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:27.290
Fuurouta, you're in the Bureau.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.750
Yeah. But I side with the kids.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.790
I was supposed to be like that too.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:41.790
The other sects aren't here yet.
 We're the first.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:44.790
Welcome.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:47.450
This is where the real war starts.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.160
Go, Aranea!

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:21.290
I'll show you how powerless you are.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.410
I believe we can change the world.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:39.900
Hey, what are you...?

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:42.270
Claude!

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:45.500
I went along with your plans
 on purpose.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:48.000
If I crush you now, people will know.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.000
Superhumans are ultimate. Saviors!

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.040
You're ditching the battery?

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.200
There's no way
 Aranea can move like that.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.080
The same as Jiro?

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.290
As strong as Equus?

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:15.950
I read the report about Claude.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:20.120
He has an unknown energy force
 and can convert metals.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.830
But you weren't satisfied with it.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:25.200
What we wanted was Jiro Hitoyoshi.

00:15:25.250 --> 00:15:29.490
But Jiro was just a coincidence.
 There aren't two of him.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:32.870
But we still need that power.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:37.370
That's why you sacrificed
 many superhumans to make Claude.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:40.620
Or rather, you made that helmet.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:44.450
He's amplifying his power
 with that helmet.

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.080
Temporarily.

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:50.040
I'm sorry for your suffering
 at Ogasawara.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:53.750
But did you have to
 rile up the students?

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:57.700
Of course. This is war, Jiro.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:00.120
Superhumans against humans.

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.250
Superhumans aren't human's foe.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.440
Superhumans protect humans.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.940
But who protects superhumans?
 The Bureau?

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.620
When have you protected us, Jiro?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.160
Kikko.

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.040
How dare you call me by name.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.910
You desire war too?

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.410
My only aim is to protect Jiro-san.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.500
No weapons?

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:31.880
Of course not.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:34.510
I can transport too.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:43.980
I want to kill you,
 but I promised him.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.690
You looked up to superhumans too.

00:16:49.330 --> 00:16:51.070
Those that know what's right.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:55.000
Not for oneself nor the country.
 But just one...

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.290
Just one what?

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.370
Justice? Peace? Freedom?

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.410
Jin.

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.910
Protecting my freedom
 will disrupt peace.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:07.710
Pursuing your justice will
 violate my freedom.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.090
There's no single answer.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:13.660
If you say it's for humans,
 we must fight them now.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:16.870
And make a world where
 superhumans don't suffer.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:35.030
You'll be fine now.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:39.830
Superhumans protect humans,
 and humans thank them.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.160
That's just a fantasy, Jiro.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:45.330
Still, I want to believe.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:50.290
That the superhumans I looked up to
 as a kid exist somewhere.

00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:53.300
I want to be able to protect them.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.670
Be a hero of justice.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:58.040
Jiro Senpai.

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.300
No, Jiro.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.750
Jiro, your words sound pleasing.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.790
That's because they're fantasies.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.690
Dreams and ideals that will
 never come true.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:11.000
I was told to become another you.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:15.070
I will. I'll crush you and
 become the only one.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:17.040
Lock one.

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:19.120
I'm not your replacement.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.910
Lock two.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:22.080
No!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.830
I deny every bit of you!

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:27.370
Your freedom, peace,
 justice, everything!

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.500
Lock three!

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:42.430
Is that the true you?

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.540
Jiro!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:06.830
Out of my way.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:16.830
Wait, hold on.

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:19.040
The helmet's broken.
 I can't control...

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:21.870
My power...

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.790
Just Japan's internal problems now.

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:34.770
Jiro.

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:37.250
Do you despise me?

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:41.700
Only Ogre Emi can stop that.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:47.540
Somebody, save Jiro.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.450
Jiro-san?

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:55.080
Why should we help the Bureau?

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:19.750
"S" Planetarian?

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.500
Another one of the same type?

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:24.540
You saved me.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.120
Not just me.

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:32.080
Come on, y'all!

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:34.620
You're official superhumans, right?

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:42.290
Open the door to this heart

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:46.370
Right now, a nice season...

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.370
Should I stop time? But...

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:51.790
You're of the Bureau, right?
 What should we do?

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.190
Equus is sucking power from Jiro.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.370
We have to pull him out. But...

00:20:58.250 --> 00:20:59.190
Got it.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:09.530
Over here!

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:07.500
And so, the Revised Secret
 Functional Law

00:22:07.580 --> 00:22:09.970
has just now been voted down!

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:15.500
You suddenly changed your mind,
 and it was rejected.

00:22:15.540 --> 00:22:18.500
Did the Shinjuku riot scare you?

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:20.860
Councilor Mitsuya, answer us!

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:23.160
It's the Chief Secretary.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:28.240
The boss, Mr. Akita,
 will never forgive you.

00:22:29.870 --> 00:22:31.240
Sir Mitsuya.

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.620
You betrayed us.

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:39.540
To think we could guide superhumans
 and humans with our powers.

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:41.540
It was arrogant.

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:44.620
Is it you, Akita?

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:47.090
You killed Mitsuya and took his body.

00:22:47.370 --> 00:22:50.330
If our alien brothers found out...

00:22:51.080 --> 00:22:55.410
The Revised Secret Functional Law
 that was predicted to pass was...

00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:56.700
Um...

00:22:57.450 --> 00:23:01.080
Are you sure Jiro Senpai
 didn't leave any messages?

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:04.700
Councilor Mitsuya changed his mind
 at the last minute.

00:23:04.750 --> 00:23:07.410
It seems many
 other councilors followed.

00:23:07.830 --> 00:23:11.540
As for his reason for voting no...

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:16.000
So he kept his promise never to see
 Hoshinoko again.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:19.200
I'd meant for him to chuck her out.

00:25:23.410 --> 00:25:26.000
(August, the 20th of Shinka Era
 Hiroshima)

00:25:26.580 --> 00:25:29.000
November, the 46th of Shinka Era.

00:25:29.040 --> 00:25:32.000
An era when superhumans are
 being deprived of freedom.

00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:36.450
Wanting to protect them, Jiro
 Hitoyoshi chose to be a fugitive.

00:25:36.580 --> 00:25:38.410
Is justice only a fantasy?

00:25:38.450 --> 00:25:40.830
Concrete Revolutio,
 Superhuman Phantasmagoria.
